.nh
.TH "LAGO" "1" "Sep 2026" "Lago CLI" "Lago CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
lago-billable-metrics-create - Create a billable metric


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlago billable-metrics create [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
This endpoint creates a new billable metric representing a pricing component of your application.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--aggregation-type\fP=""
	Aggregation method used to compute usage for this billable metric.; one of: count_agg, sum_agg, max_agg, unique_count_agg, weighted_sum_agg, latest_agg

.PP
\fB--code\fP=""
	Unique code used to identify the billable metric associated with the API request. This code associates each event with the correct metric.

.PP
\fB--description\fP=""
	Internal description of the billable metric.

.PP
\fB--expression\fP=""
	Expression used to calculate the event units. The expression is evalutated for each event and the result is then used to calculate the total aggregated units.
Accepted function are 'ceil', 'concat' and 'round' as well as '+', '-', '\\' and '*' operations.
Round is accepting an optional second parameter to specify the number of decimal.

.PP
\fB--field-name\fP=""
	Property of the billable metric used for aggregating usage data. This field is not required for 'count_agg'.

.PP
\fB--filters\fP=""
	API field (array)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for create

.PP
\fB--input\fP=""
	Complete JSON request body or @file.json

.PP
\fB--name\fP=""
	Name of the billable metric.

.PP
\fB--recurring\fP=""
	Defines if the billable metric is persisted billing period over billing period.
.IP \(bu 2
If set to 'true': the accumulated number of units calculated from the previous billing period is persisted to the next billing period.
.IP \(bu 2
If set to 'false': the accumulated number of units is reset to 0 at the end of the billing period.
.IP \(bu 2
If not defined in the request, default value is 'false'.

.PP
\fB--rounding-function\fP=""
	Refers to the numeric value or mathematical expression that will be rounded based on the calculated number of billing units. Possible values are 'round', 'ceil' and 'floor'.; one of: ceil, floor, round,

.PP
\fB--rounding-precision\fP=""
	Specifies the number of decimal places to which the 'rounding_function' will be rounded. It can be a positive or negative value.

.PP
\fB--weighted-interval\fP=""
	Parameter exclusively utilized in conjunction with the 'weighted_sum' aggregation type. It serves to adjust the aggregation result by assigning weights and proration to the result based on time intervals. When this field is not provided, the default time interval is assumed to be in 'seconds'.; one of: seconds,


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	Override the Lago API key

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Override the Lago API URL

.PP
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	Confirm a dangerous operation with its resource identifier

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print mutating requests without sending them

.PP
\fB--insecure\fP[=false]
	Allow insecure HTTP or TLS for self-hosted Lago

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	Environment mode: live or test

.PP
\fB--no-retry\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic retries

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format: table, json, or yaml

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	Named profile to use

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath expression applied to the response

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Total request timeout

.PP
\fB--timing\fP[=false]
	Print request latency breakdown

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Print redacted request and response details


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  lago billable-metrics create --input @payload.json
  lago billable-metrics create --input @payload.json --output json  # full resource
.EE


